From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hefesto DualSense4Unix Project <hefesto-dualsense4unix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_hid: size GET_REPORT responses to the stored
 report

get_report_workqueue_handler() answers a GET_REPORT with

	req->zero = 0;
	req->length = min(wLength, report_length, MAX_REPORT_LENGTH);

so the response is always as long as the smallest of the three, and never as
long as the report userspace stored with GADGET_HID_WRITE_GET_REPORT, even
though struct usb_hidg_report carries a @length documented as "length of the
report response". With a report descriptor whose feature reports are shorter
than 64 bytes and a host that asks for more, the response is padded to 64
bytes, which fills the ep0 packets exactly (maxpacket 64), and since
req->zero is cleared no zero-length packet ends the data stage. The host
keeps waiting for the rest of the transfer until its control timeout.

That host is a common one: SDL's HIDAPI backend and Wine's winebus read
feature reports through HIDIOCGFEATURE with a 128-byte buffer, and hidraw
passes that size on as wLength. Measured on a Pop!_OS 24.04 machine
(7.1.5) with four DualSense-compatible gadgets on usbip-vudc and vhci-hcd: every
HIDIOCGFEATURE(128) on a gadget hidraw returned -ETIMEDOUT after ~5.1 s, for
every feature report, while a real DualSense on the same host answers the
41-byte and 20-byte reports with a short packet in milliseconds. Four pads
times a handful of feature reports times 5 s does not fit in the 10 s that
Wine's services.exe gives winebus to start, so a game under Proton started
with no controller at all.

End the response at the stored report length when it is shorter, and ask
for a zero-length packet whenever the response is shorter than wLength, so
the data stage is always terminated. Both the immediate path and the path
that waits for userspace size the request the same way. When nothing was
stored for the report id, the length is unchanged (the zeroed buffer).

With the patch the same HIDIOCGFEATURE(128) calls return 41, 20 and 64 bytes
in 2-6 ms on all four gadgets, with no timeouts.

Also expose a read-only module parameter, get_report_sized, that is always
Y. Nothing else in sysfs tells this module from one without the change, and
userspace serving feature reports to such a host needs to know. The sizing
itself never reads the parameter.

Signed-off-by: Hefesto DualSense4Unix Project <hefesto-dualsense4unix@users.noreply.github.com>
---
  drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c |   31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
  1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c
@@ -30,6 +30,20 @@
  */
 #define GET_REPORT_TIMEOUT_MS 2500
 
+/*
+ * Read-only mark for the GET_REPORT response sizing in
+ * f_hidg_size_get_report(). Nothing else in sysfs tells a module that ends
+ * the response at the stored report length from one that pads it to 64 bytes
+ * without a zero-length packet, and userspace that serves feature reports to
+ * a host with a 128-byte wLength (SDL HIDAPI, Wine's winebus) needs to know:
+ * over the unpatched module every such request waits for the host timeout.
+ * The sizing itself never reads the parameter.
+ */
+static bool get_report_sized = true;
+module_param(get_report_sized, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(get_report_sized,
+		 "GET_REPORT responses end at the stored report length, with a zero-length packet when they fill ep0 packets (always Y)");
+
 static int major, minors;
 
 static const struct class hidg_class = {
@@ -555,6 +569,20 @@
 	return NULL;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The response is as long as the report userspace stored (its @length), and a
+ * response shorter than the host's wLength ends with a zero-length packet when
+ * it fills ep0 packets exactly: without it the host waits for the rest until
+ * its control timeout (5 s in usbhid).
+ */
+static void f_hidg_size_get_report(struct f_hidg *hidg, struct usb_request *req,
+				   struct report_entry *ptr)
+{
+	if (ptr && ptr->report_data.length && ptr->report_data.length < req->length)
+		req->length = ptr->report_data.length;
+	req->zero = req->length < hidg->get_report_req_report_length;
+}
+
 static void get_report_workqueue_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct f_hidg *hidg = container_of(work, struct f_hidg, work);
@@ -572,7 +600,6 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
-	req->zero = 0;
 	req->length = min_t(unsigned int, min_t(unsigned int, hidg->get_report_req_report_length,
 							      hidg->report_length),
 					  MAX_REPORT_LENGTH);
@@ -582,6 +609,7 @@
 	if (ptr && !ptr->report_data.userspace_req) {
 		/* Report exists in list and it is to be used for immediate response */
 		req->buf = ptr->report_data.data;
+		f_hidg_size_get_report(hidg, req, ptr);
 		status = usb_ep_queue(cdev->gadget->ep0, req, GFP_ATOMIC);
 		hidg->get_report_returned = true;
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hidg->get_report_spinlock, flags);
@@ -622,6 +650,7 @@
 			req->buf = hidg->get_report.data;
 			memset(req->buf, 0x0, req->length);
 		}
+		f_hidg_size_get_report(hidg, req, ptr);
 
 		status = usb_ep_queue(cdev->gadget->ep0, req, GFP_ATOMIC);
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hidg->get_report_spinlock, flags);
-- 
2.43.0

